  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.25,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.22 from 6 h onward. If the reader were saturating, diluted aliquots would read much higher than the undiluted value once the dilution factor was applied. The 18 h aliquot did not do this. The dilution-corrected values were 1.35 (10x, n=2), 1.26 (20x, n=2) and 1.17 (40x, n=1), against 1.209 undiluted. They have no consistent upward trend with dilution and the mean is only about 3% above the undiluted reading, which is within noise. The 6 h control (10x gave 1.213 against 1.236 undiluted) shows the reader is linear at this OD. The plateau therefore looks like genuine stationary phase, and the biomass is as read."
  },
